        "consecutiveClarify": 0,
        "consecutiveNoProgress": 0,
        "lastCandidateQuestion": "Thank you. I'd like to keep going, honestly — it helps to have something to work on.\n\nSo, back to COGS. If we don't have the input-level split yet, my working assumption is that the increase is concentrated in coffee beans, since that's typically the largest single input and green coffee prices have been volatile. Sixteen points of revenue is a large move for packaging or dairy alone.\n\nThe other thing I'd test is whether it's price or volume. If bean cost per pound went up, that's a sourcing and contract issue. If pounds used per drink went up, that's waste or portioning — spoilage, remakes, over-pouring.\n\nDo we have cost per pound of coffee for both years, and roughly what share of COGS beans represent?",
